{
 "v": "aumlok-proper-names-v2",
 "what": "The proper-name, place and brand list the AUMLOK lists and the DRAWN-PHRASE arms of the courts are checked against, so a name cannot re-enter silently.",
 "rule": "Two tiers, because one rule could not catch the words Peter met. (1) RULE-BASED, the `words` list: a name is dropped when it is in the dictionary's own propernames list, or is a brand word, AND has NO common lowercase dictionary entry of its own. This is the precise form: it drops john, santa and nicky, and keeps art, case, list and guy, because the dictionary defines those as ordinary words. (2) BY NAME, the `places` and `ambiguousNames` lists: these drop unconditionally, WITHOUT the common-sense guard. A place or a surname reads as one whatever else the dictionary says about the spelling, and the guard is what let `manila` ship — the dictionary defines a manila (the paper, the hemp), so the rule kept a word that reads as a city. `smith` is the surname case X2 names, and `manila` is the place case the common-words court caught.",
 "limits": "NOT complete, and it does not claim to be. It catches names the dictionary knows and the places and surnames written here, and it cannot catch a name neither carries — `tucson` is in neither /usr/share/dict/words nor /usr/share/dict/propernames, and it is dropped only because it is written into `places`. This file is a curated judgment list, not a published register of names. That is precisely why EFF-only sourcing does the real work here and this list is the backstop, not the mechanism: EFF is ordinary English and some of its nouns double as names, so the construction removes the corpus source of names without removing all names. The list also costs real words: `turkey`, `china` and `chile` are dropped as places, and they are also ordinary nouns. That is the deliberate trade — as one of seven life-words, TURKEY reads as a country first.",
 "sources": [
  {
   "name": "the local dictionary's propernames list",
   "path": "/usr/share/dict/propernames",
   "role": "rule-based: a first name with no common lowercase dictionary entry of its own"
  },
  {
   "name": "place and brand words",
   "path": "plugins/aukora-aumlok/data/safety/category-drop.json",
   "role": "rule-based: brand spellings the category drop already names"
  },
  {
   "name": "curated places (this file's `places`)",
   "role": "CURATED, NOT PUBLISHED: countries, US states and major cities written out for this repository, including `tucson`, which no list on this machine carries"
  },
  {
   "name": "curated ambiguous surnames (this file's `ambiguousNames`)",
   "role": "CURATED, NOT PUBLISHED: ordinary English words that are also among the commonest surnames, dropped because of how they read in an identity phrase"
  }
 ],
